              "type": "text",
              "name": "사용자 텍스트 1",
              "text": "The city grew quiet after midnight, when shop lights faded and every sound carried farther than expected. She walked without a destination, collecting details along the way: a bent street sign, the smell of rain on concrete, a radio playing behind an open window, and the faint comfort of knowing that someone else nearby was still awake too.\n\nBy morning, the streets would return to their old rhythm, crowded with deliveries, hurried conversations, and people moving toward plans they had made days ago. None of them would notice the chalk mark beside the station entrance or the paper crane tucked beneath the bench, yet those little signs mattered to her. They proved that the night had not been empty, that a private world could exist between one normal day and the next. She never expected anyone to understand why she kept looking for them. It was enough that they appeared, quietly and without explanation, whenever she was close to giving up.",
